# EduFlow — Cursor Rules
# BuildwithAiGiri MVP #15

## Project
- Product: EduFlow — AI-powered school management OS with configurable workflows
- Stack: Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- AI: Gemini 2.0 Flash (primary) → OpenRouter claude-3-haiku (fallback)
- Theme: Dark neural/cyberpunk — bg #030014, cyan #00d4ff, purple #7c3aed

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript strictly — no `any` unless absolutely necessary
- Prefer functional components and hooks
- Use Tailwind utility classes; avoid arbitrary inline style overrides unless needed for dynamic colors
- Keep components in /src/app — no separate /components folder for MVP
- "use client" only when required (interactivity, hooks)

## Design System
- Background: #030014 (neural-bg)
- Surface: #0d0a2e (neural-surface)
- Border: #1e1b4b (neural-border)
- Cyan: #00d4ff (neural-cyan) — primary CTAs, triggers
- Purple: #7c3aed (neural-purple) — AI features, conditions
- Green: #22c55e (neural-green) — success, actions
- Amber: #f59e0b (neural-amber) — warnings, fees

## Workflow Node Colors
- Trigger nodes: cyan border
- Condition nodes: amber border
- Action nodes: green border

## API
- All AI calls go through /api/ai-tools
- Try Gemini first, fallback to OpenRouter, then mock
- Never expose API keys in client code

## School Domain
- Primary market: India (INR pricing, WhatsApp-first)
- Secondary: Global EdTech
- Key workflows: Attendance Alert, Fee Escalation, Admission Pipeline
- Mock school: Greenfield International School, 847 students
